# VS Code REST Client: run requests individually from top to bottom.
# Passwords are prompted at send time; this file contains no working credentials.
# Use the Admin email provisioned with npm run admin:create.
# The create-user step creates a REAL account. Change userEmail to an unused email.
# Upload uses REAL existing local files. Sections 4-13 demonstrate image preparation
# and manual review. Sections V1-V8 demonstrate actual joint-five-frame video OCR.
# Both profiles are available with config/pipelines.kaggle.json when ready.
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:3000
@adminEmail = admin@example.com
@userEmail = reviewer@example.com
@pipelineId = pbl6-yolo11l-botsort-prepare-v1
@ocrPipelineId = pbl6-resnet34c-joint5-v1

### Database/schema readiness (does not check ML or the worker)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### 1. Admin login
# @name adminLogin
# @prompt password Enter the existing Admin password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2. Admin creates a User (choose the password; at least 12 characters)
# @name createUser
# @prompt password Choose a password for this User (12+ characters)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "display_name": "Plate reviewer",
  "role": "user"
}

### 3. User login (enter the password chosen above)
# @name userLogin
# @prompt password Enter the User password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Current User and role
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 4. Upload an image
# @name uploadMedia
# @prompt imagePath Absolute path to an existing JPG image (use forward slashes on Windows)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/media
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=plate-recognition-boundary

--plate-recognition-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="plate-source.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< {{imagePath}}
--plate-recognition-boundary--

### List this User's sources
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/media?limit=50&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Read the exact uploaded source
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/media/{{uploadMedia.response.body.$.id}}/content
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 5. Check readiness. Continue to job creation only when selected profile is ready.
# Prepare needs the detector, Python and Pipeline repo; it does not need OCR.
# Joint-five-frame OCR also needs the pinned Kaggle checkpoint. Check media_types.
# Missing required resources => ready=false; job creation then returns 503.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/pipelines
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 6. Create an asynchronous prepare job; 202 returns job_id
# @name createJob
# scene detects plates in the source; change to plate_crop only for a pre-cropped image.
# Video uploads must use scene (change upload filename/MIME to match the actual video).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-jobs
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "media_id": "{{uploadMedia.response.body.$.id}}",
  "pipeline_id": "{{pipelineId}}",
  "input_mode": "scene"
}

### 7. Poll until succeeded or failed; worker must run in another terminal
# @name jobStatus
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-jobs/{{createJob.response.body.$.job_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 8. Results; 409 until succeeded. Stop the review flow if items is empty.
# @name jobResults
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-jobs/{{createJob.response.body.$.job_id}}/results?limit=50&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 9. Inspect first result, predictions, evidence URLs and review history
# @name resultDetail
# Re-send this GET before every review so expected_revision stays current.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-results/{{jobResults.response.body.$.items[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Read first crop (when detections is nonempty)
GET {{baseUrl}}{{resultDetail.response.body.$.detections[0].crop_url}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Read first keyframe (only if frame_url is non-null)
GET {{baseUrl}}{{resultDetail.response.body.$.detections[0].frame_url}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 10A. Confirm machine text ONLY when a recognize profile returned readable text
# Choose ONE review action; a second action needs a refreshed resultDetail first.
# The image prepare profile has machine_status=not_run: SKIP this request and use 10B.
# A machine result without readable text cannot be confirmed (422).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-results/{{resultDetail.response.body.$.id}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "confirm",
  "note": "Checked against source evidence",
  "expected_revision": {{resultDetail.response.body.$.revision}}
}

### 10B. Enter plate text manually for prepare (or correct OCR output)
# Refresh resultDetail before sending if any review has already been submitted.
# @prompt correctedPlate Enter the plate text read from the evidence
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-results/{{resultDetail.response.body.$.id}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "correct",
  "corrected_text": "{{correctedPlate}}",
  "note": "Plate text read manually from source evidence",
  "expected_revision": {{resultDetail.response.body.$.revision}}
}

### 10C. Mark unreadable instead (refresh resultDetail before sending)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-results/{{resultDetail.response.body.$.id}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "unreadable",
  "expected_revision": {{resultDetail.response.body.$.revision}}
}

### 10D. Reject a false detection or wrongly merged track instead
# Refresh resultDetail before sending. No corrected_text is allowed for reject.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-results/{{resultDetail.response.body.$.id}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "reject",
  "note": "False detection or incorrect track association",
  "expected_revision": {{resultDetail.response.body.$.revision}}
}

### 11. History remains in result detail; machine predictions remain unchanged
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-results/{{jobResults.response.body.$.items[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 12. Search current normalized effective text
# @prompt searchPlate Enter a plate to search (uppercase, without spaces or hyphens)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-results?plate={{searchPlate}}&limit=50&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Pending results of the latest successful business job for this source
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-results?media_id={{uploadMedia.response.body.$.id}}&review_status=pending&limit=50&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Job history for this source, including prior runs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-jobs?media_id={{uploadMedia.response.body.$.id}}&limit=50&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 13. Export this successful job as CSV
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-jobs/{{createJob.response.body.$.job_id}}/export?format=csv
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### V1. Upload a video for the joint-five-frame OCR model
# @name uploadVideo
# @prompt videoPath Absolute path to an existing MP4 video (forward slashes on Windows)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/media
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=plate-video-boundary

--plate-video-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="plate-video.mp4"
Content-Type: video/mp4

< {{videoPath}}
--plate-video-boundary--

### V2. Create real OCR job; the selected profile must be ready
# @name createOcrJob
# Only video + scene is supported by this profile; an image returns 422.
# Each eligible track supplies five real crops from five distinct ordered frames.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-jobs
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "media_id": "{{uploadVideo.response.body.$.id}}",
  "pipeline_id": "{{ocrPipelineId}}",
  "input_mode": "scene"
}

### V3. Poll until succeeded or failed; inspect statistics and errors
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-jobs/{{createOcrJob.response.body.$.job_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### V4. OCR results; 409 until succeeded
# @name ocrResults
# An empty items array is valid if no track had five eligible frames; skip V5-V7.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-jobs/{{createOcrJob.response.body.$.job_id}}/results?limit=50&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### V5. Inspect machine text, five evidence images and joint prediction
# @name ocrDetail
# predictions is at result level, each with five ordered detection_ids.
# recognition_method=joint_multiframe; agreement_count and ocr_score are null.
# frame_weights describe learned feature fusion; they are not confidence or votes.
# Re-send this GET before each review to obtain the current revision.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-results/{{ocrResults.response.body.$.items[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Read a selected OCR crop; inspect indices 0..4 and their source frames before review
GET {{baseUrl}}{{ocrDetail.response.body.$.detections[0].crop_url}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Read the crop's source frame (only if frame_url is non-null)
GET {{baseUrl}}{{ocrDetail.response.body.$.detections[0].frame_url}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### V6. Confirm ONLY readable text checked against all source evidence
# Choose V6 or V7; refresh ocrDetail before making a second review.
# Use unreadable/reject actions instead when appropriate (see image flow above).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-results/{{ocrDetail.response.body.$.id}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "confirm",
  "note": "Checked plate text and track association against all five source frames",
  "expected_revision": {{ocrDetail.response.body.$.revision}}
}

### V7. Correct the OCR text instead; machine prediction stays immutable
# @prompt correctedOcrPlate Enter the correct plate text from the source evidence
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-results/{{ocrDetail.response.body.$.id}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "action": "correct",
  "corrected_text": "{{correctedOcrPlate}}",
  "note": "Corrected after inspecting the five source frames",
  "expected_revision": {{ocrDetail.response.body.$.revision}}
}

### V8. Export OCR machine text, effective text, review state and temporal locations
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/recognition-jobs/{{createOcrJob.response.body.$.job_id}}/export?format=csv
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 14. User logout (run after completing the desired flows; revokes the token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Admin logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.$.access_token}}
